  #line-at(92.76pt, 202.2pt, "Highlights  ")
  #line-at(126pt, 225.48pt, "A millimetric post raises the Leidenfrost point by 20℃ compared to a flat surface  ")
  #line-at(126pt, 240pt, "The post promotes two modes of temperature-dependent droplet breakup ")
  #line-at(126pt, 254.4pt, "For nucleate boiling, the post increases the droplet cooling capacity by up to 24% ")
  #line-at(126pt, 268.8pt, "When inclined, the post prevents droplet sliding and rebound, increasing heat transfer  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 312.12pt, "Abstract ")
  #line-at(90pt, 333.84pt, "This study experimentally explores fluid breakup and Leidenfrost dynamics for droplets impacting ")
  #line-at(90pt, 347.52pt, "a heated millimetric post. Using high-speed optical and infrared imaging, we investigate the droplet ")
  #line-at(90pt, 361.2pt, "lifetime, breakup and boiling modes, as well as the cooling performance of different substrates. The ")
  #line-at(90pt, 374.76pt, "post substrate leads to a shorter droplet lifetime and a 20 ℃ higher Leidenfrost temperature ")
  #line-at(90pt, 388.44pt, "compared to a flat substrate, attributed to mixed boiling modes along the height of the post and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 402.12pt, "additional pinning. For temperatures below the Leidenfrost point, in the nucleate boiling regime, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 415.8pt, "the post substrate also provides a larger maximum temperature drop than its flat counterpart. The ")
  #line-at(90pt, 429.48pt, "enhanced cooling capacity can be attributed to better droplet pinning and an enlarged droplet-")
  #line-at(90pt, 443.04pt, "substrate contact area. The post’s superior cooling performance becomes especially clear for impact ")
  #line-at(90pt, 456.72pt, "on an inclined surface, where the post successfully prevents the rolling and bouncing of the droplet, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 470.4pt, "providing a 51% to 180% increase in the maximum local temperature drop. Interestingly, at ")
  #line-at(90pt, 484.08pt, "temperatures slightly above the Leidenfrost point and for a relatively narrow range of Weber ")
  #line-at(90pt, 497.64pt, "numbers, droplets on the post substrate rebound rather than break up due to a complex interplay of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 511.32pt, "inertial, capillary, and bubble (thin film) dynamics. Overall, the findings show that a large-scale ")
  #line-at(90pt, 525pt, "structure increases the Leidenfrost temperature and enhances droplet breakup and interfacial heat ")
  #line-at(90pt, 538.56pt, "transfer efficiency during non-isothermal droplet impact. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 560.16pt, "Keywords: Droplet impact, Leidenfrost, fin, pinning, nucleate boiling ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 15.93pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 634.08pt, "1")
  #line-at(111.6pt, 634.08pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(108pt, 648.96pt, "Research on droplets impacting heated surfaces is motivated by various applications such as ")
  #line-at(90pt, 661.56pt, "spray cooling [1, 2] and internal combustion engines [3, 4]. During such non-isothermal droplet ")
  #line-at(90pt, 674.28pt, "impact, the hydrodynamics and heat transfer are strongly influenced by the surface temperature [5]. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 686.88pt, "At the lowest temperatures, droplet dynamics and phase change are mostly decoupled, with contact-")
  #line-at(90pt, 699.6pt, "line-dominated evaporation taking place after droplet deposition [6, 7]. When the surface ")
  #line-at(90pt, 712.2pt, "temperature is higher than the liquid saturation point, the droplet undergoes nucleate boiling and ")
]

