#original-page(612pt, 792pt, (image("graphics/page-03.png", width: 14pt), 307.5pt, 676.5pt))[
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 81.96pt, "components. However, to the best of the authors’ knowledge, the combined effect of droplet impact ")
  #line-at(90pt, 94.56pt, "dynamics, heat transfer, and Leidenfrost dynamics on a heated large-scale structure remains ")
  #line-at(90pt, 107.28pt, "unknown. In this study, we thus investigated non-isothermal droplet impact and Leidenfrost ")
  #line-at(90pt, 119.88pt, "dynamics on a single post structure on an aluminum surface, which is easily fabricated using ")
  #line-at(90pt, 132.6pt, "traditional machining methods, and compared them to impact on a flat surface. The droplet lifetime ")
  #line-at(90pt, 145.2pt, "and the static Leidenfrost temperature were analyzed. Typical droplet impact and boiling modes, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 157.8pt, "as well as the breakup morphologies, were observed and classified for Weber numbers ranging ")
  #line-at(90pt, 170.52pt, "from 10 to 120 and surface temperatures between 120 ℃ and 330 ℃. The cooling effect of the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 183.12pt, "droplets on the substrates was also quantified by measuring the transient temperature distribution ")
  #line-at(90pt, 195.84pt, "at the bottom of the thin substrates using high-speed infrared (IR) imaging. In addition, droplet ")
  #line-at(90pt, 208.44pt, "dynamics and heat transfer characteristics on an inclined surface were compared to highlight the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 221.04pt, "important contribution of pinning at the post structure on enhancing the cooling efficiency.   ")
