  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 382.56pt, "So far, we have discussed droplet dynamics and cooling capacities for droplets centrally impacting ")
  #line-at(90pt, 396.24pt, "the post right. In real-world droplet impingement applications, however, off-center impact is more ")
  #line-at(90pt, 409.8pt, "likely, for which the benefit of the post structure, which prevents sliding and bounding of the droplet, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 423.48pt, "might be diminished. To provide guidelines on the applicability of millimetric surface patterning, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 437.16pt, "we also investigated the off-center impact on the post substrate, and found that the post structure ")
  #line-at(90pt, 450.84pt, "(1 mm in diameter) can still prevent the sliding of the droplet with an impact location of up to 1.6 ")
  #line-at(90pt, 464.4pt, "mm (horizontal distance) downhill from the center of the post. Detailed information on droplet ")
  #line-at(90pt, 477.96pt, "dynamics for off-center impact is provided in Supplementary Material Section 10.  ")
  #line-at(90pt, 499.68pt, "In addition to the here-presented inclination angle of 30° and Weber number of ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(445.32pt, 499.68pt, "We")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(459.36pt, 499.68pt, " = 65, we also ")
  #line-at(90pt, 513.36pt, "investigated to the effect of droplet pinning on the cooling capacity for different inclination angles, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 527.04pt, "substrate temperatures, and Weber numbers. Detailed information and results can also be found in ")
  #line-at(90pt, 540.6pt, "Supplementary Material Section 10.  ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 15.93pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 571.2pt, "4")
  #line-at(111.6pt, 571.2pt, "Conclusion ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 586.2pt, "This study experimentally explored hydrodynamics and heat transfer during droplet impact on a ")
  #line-at(90pt, 599.88pt, "millimetric heated post. Detailed analyses have been carried out on droplet lifetime, boiling modes, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 613.32pt, "and cooling capacity. We can draw the following conclusions: ")
  #line-at(108pt, 635.16pt, "1)")
  #line-at(126pt, 635.16pt, "The post substrate shows a 20 ℃ higher Leidenfrost temperature compared to the flat ")
  #line-at(126pt, 648.84pt, "substrate, which is attributed to a mixed boiling mode and additional pinning induced by ")
  #line-at(126pt, 662.4pt, "the post.    ")
  #line-at(108pt, 676.08pt, "2)")
  #line-at(126pt, 676.08pt, "Six different droplet impact and boiling modes were identified for initial substrate ")
  #line-at(126pt, 689.76pt, "temperatures ranging from 120 ℃ to 330 ℃ and Weber numbers between 10 and 120: 1) ")
  #line-at(126pt, 703.44pt, "deposition, 2) atomization, 3) rebound with atomization, 4) breakup with atomization, 5) ")
  #line-at(126pt, 717pt, "rebound, and 6) breakup. ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(239.04pt, 717pt, "We")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(253.08pt, 717pt, "-")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(256.56pt, 717pt, "T")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 6.947pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(262.8pt, 717.96pt, "S")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(266.64pt, 717pt, " regime maps were constructed to quantify the differences ")
]

