  #line-at(186.84pt, 553.8pt, "*")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(190.08pt, 557.76pt, " =0.3). As a result, the vapor pushes the liquid-solid contact line away from ")
  #line-at(90pt, 571.44pt, "the post, leading to a much larger apparent liquid-solid interface area compared to the flat substrate, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 585pt, "where foaming is absent. This increase in the contact area enhances the heat transfer, leading to the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 598.68pt, "observed shorter droplet lifetime (Fig. 2 of main article) and lower surface temperature (Fig. 7 of ")
  #line-at(90pt, 612.24pt, "main article) on the post substrate.    ")
  #line-at(90pt, 633.96pt, "At ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(104.52pt, 633.96pt, "Ts")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(114.96pt, 633.96pt, " = 150℃ (b), the boiling is vigorous and chaotic on both substrates. The droplet surface is ")
  #line-at(90pt, 647.64pt, "deformed heavily by the intense vapor generation and the atomization near the liquid rim. Except ")
