  #line-at(360.72pt, 130.2pt, "S")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(364.56pt, 129.24pt, ". A strong temperature drop can be ")
  #line-at(90pt, 142.92pt, "identified once a new droplet impacts the substrate, followed by a recovery as the droplet evaporates. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 156.48pt, "However, if the volume flow rate is much larger than the evaporation rate, the droplets can grow to ")
  #line-at(90pt, 170.16pt, "a very large water body (a water pool). Then, for these flooded samples, we can expect that both ")
  #line-at(90pt, 183.84pt, "the temperature drop and its recovery will be smaller due to the slow temperature change of the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 197.52pt, "water pool. For ")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(161.4pt, 197.52pt, "T")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 6.947pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(167.52pt, 198.48pt, "S")
  #set text(font: ("Times New Roman", "New Computer Modern Math"), size: 11.019pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(171.36pt, 197.52pt, " = 110℃, where the volume flow rate was low enough to prevent flooding, the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 211.08pt, "temperature of the post substrate was always lower than that of the flat substrate, indicating that ")
  #line-at(90pt, 224.76pt, "the post structure continuously increases the heat transfer in this temperature range and enables an ")
  #line-at(90pt, 238.44pt, "efficient increase in cooling capacity. For ")
